=====================  rozOS RESCUE MODE  =====================
The root file system on the disk could not be used, so this small
rescue system runs from memory (what you change here is lost at
power off). Your files may still be on the disk - try:
  ls /dev ; mount                sda2 = the rozOS root; a pen drive is on /mnt/usb
  mount /dev/sda2 /mnt/disk      try the disk by hand (ls /mnt/disk/home)
  cd /mnt/disk ; tar -cf /mnt/usb/home.tar home     save your files to a pen drive
  kinstall -l   then   kinstall -d factory  and  reboot   (another kernel)
  help rescue                    step by step
Full system: boot the ISO, or on the PC: make disk-check / make disk-update
